/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T11:44:09-07:00","id":1465022,"title":"","content":"A for me. Very close with the Fae Touched though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T19:54:38-07:00","id":1465235,"title":"","content":"Gonna go with D this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T17:28:20-07:00","id":1465454,"title":"","content":"D! D! D! D! D!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T09:11:37-07:00","id":1493831,"title":"","content":"<i>I have owed you this for far too long. IIRC, Fae-Touched and Stigmatic ended up tying in the end, but Fae-Touched was in the lead first, so that's the one I wrote up first.<br /> <br /> Old Man Mackenzie at one point had a much more pessimistic backstory where his grandkids were grown up and joined the Vigil and he was very much in He Who Fights Monsters territory... but I ended up not going that direction in the end. You still could though .</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alexander Mackenzie was a mean old git before he became a Hunter. Not in a cruel way, but in the way of people who lived hard lives and never got to work through their emotions. His Pa died in France soon after he was born, exploded by a German shell, and it wasn't an easy time for his Mum to raise a kid on her own in Musselburgh with another on the way. Alex was a bright kid, but he never finished school, dropping out to pick up work to feed the family. He had no time for fools or charlatans, and would not spare the feelings of either. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By all accounts, Mr. Mackenzie mellowed on his daughter\u2019s birth. Everyone had expected him to get frustrated with the young Margret\u2019s antics, but underneath the crusty and coarse exterior, he turned out to have a gift for children. He understood they were learning about the world and appreciated their genuine curiosity. Soon, he could hardly be seen without Margret and a gaggle of her friends in tow. Twenty-odd years later when he became a grandfather, the cycle repeated and no one played harder with the little ones than old Mackenzie. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Then Margret disappeared. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Old Man Mackenzie isn't a spring chicken anymore, but he has a keen eye and iron determination. He knew the thing of lint and twine that came out of the forest wasn't his daughter, so he went into the forest, hell-bent on finding her. The trees gave way to brambles, roots, and thorns unlike anything Alexander had ever seen in his long life. It was a psychedelic trip through mind and soul, full of giant ogres and grimacing imps. Eventually, Alexander Mackenzie made his way back to reality without his daughter, but is determined to find her.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Old Man Mackenzie is a changed man - but he's still the same mean old git. He tries not to take it out on the Fetch who took Margret's place. He's keeping a mighty close eye on her, but she seems like a decent parent and is just as protective of the kids as he is. He knows his grandkids need a mother and the Fetch can't tell she's not the original, so she's just another victim in all this. Probably. He tries to ignore the nightmares where he has to shoot the thing with his daughter\u2019s face to save her children. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The big change in Mackenzie isn't the magic at his fingertips. It's that now there are things lurking in the shadows and they could come for his family at any time. He's found a batch of like minded folx around town, all touched by the supernatural and all willing to fight back. Together, they keep the Vigil through the night long to keep the shadows the hell away from their families.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Attributes:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3; Strength 1, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3; Presence 4, Manipulation 2, Composure 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Skills:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Crafts 1, Investigation 2*, Medicine 1 (First Aid), Occult 2; Drive 3 (Motorcycle), Firearms 3 (Shotgun)*, Larceny 2, Stealth 1, Survival 2; Empathy 1 (Buried Feelings, Children), Intimidation 4 (Blind Fury), Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">*Asset Skills</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Wyrd:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">0</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Glamour/per Turn:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> 10/1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Merits</b>: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Back Road Atlas, Defender, Contacts 2 (Police, Security), Face in the Crowd, Lucid Dreamer, Gut Feeling, Professional Training (Security Guard) 2, Promise of Love 3, Quick Draw (Shotgun)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Willpower:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">6</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Virtue:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Protective</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Vice:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Wrathful</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Aspirations:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Keep the grandkids out of trouble, Find Margret, Drive the goblins back into the Hedge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Touchstones: His grandchildren </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Initiative:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">+5</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Defence: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Size: </b>5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Speed:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">8</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Health: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">8</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Favoured Regalia: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Sword </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Contracts:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Might of the Terrible Brute, Overpowering Dread, Primal Glory</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9